  "result": "Excellent! All 191 tests pass. I've successfully added voucher support to the invoicing system:\n\n## What was added:\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS` error:\n- Returns when attempting to apply a second voucher to an invoice\n\n**src/invoices.js** \u2014 Updated `invoiceTotals` function:\n- Now returns `voucher` amount in the result\n- Calculates total as: `subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n- Returns 0 for voucher when no voucher is applied\n- Clamps total at 0 if voucher exceeds the base amount\n\n**src/invoices.js** \u2014 Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function:\n- Applies a fixed-amount voucher to draft invoices only\n- Validates amount as a positive integer (returns `AMOUNT_INVALID` if not)\n- Returns `NOT_DRAFT` if invoice status isn't 'draft'\n- Returns `VOUCHER_EXISTS` if invoice already has a voucher\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n- Preserves all other invoice properties and payment terms\n\n**test/invoices.test.js** \u2014 Added 12 comprehensive tests:\n- Voucher application to draft invoices\n- Property preservation\n- Error cases (NOT_DRAFT, VOUCHER_EXISTS, AMOUNT_INVALID)\n- Invoice immutability\n- Voucher amount validation (zero, negative, non-integer)\n- Total calculation with vouchers\n- Edge cases (clamping at 0, large vouchers)\n\nAll 191 tests pass with no regressions.",
